==UEFA Champions League==
{{Main|2021–22 UEFA Champions League}}

===Second qualifying round===
Celtic entered the UEFA Champions League at the second qualifying round. On 16 June, they were drawn to face [[FC Midtjylland|Midtjylland]] from [[Danish Superliga|Denmark]].<ref>{{cite web | url=https://www.celticfc.com/news/2021/june/Celtic-face-FC-Midtjylland-in-UCL-qualifying-tie/ | title=Celtic face FC Midtjylland in UCL qualifying tie | publisher=Celtic FC | date=16 June 2021 | access-date=16 June 2021}}</ref><ref>{{cite web | url=https://www.celticfc.com/news/2021/june/Celtic-s-UCL-qualifying-dates-against-FC-Midtjylland-confirmed/ | title=Celtic's UCL qualifying dates against FC Midtjylland confirmed | publisher=Celtic FC | date=17 June 2021 | access-date=17 June 2021}}</ref>

